{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 demands a causal mechanism but its mechanism only explains why shared latent causes are hard to rule out; it never specifies the causal pathway by which a shared latent cause produces apparently uncorrelated failures simultaneously across independent operators. The problem asks what evidence would distinguish truly independent failure modes from merely uncorrelated ones, but SRC_001's mechanism does not supply any discriminating causal test — it asserts that absence of shared dependencies must be proven, which is an epistemic barrier, not a causal mechanism linking observed non-correlation to latent common-cause activation. Without specifying how the latent cause propagates and produces the observed failure signature (e.g., timing, scope, conditional activation pattern), there is no mechanism to falsify or confirm independence.","target":"a2e6f3f9f482a0d8b35bca8092d97e224f2cbf8466f8337739664cbb24b2c227"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002's mechanism collapses the distinction the problem asks for by invoking an infinite-time limit in which catastrophic shared-cause probability approaches 1. But the problem concerns whether a decentralized network is more resilient under finite, operational conditions and what evidence distinguishes independent from merely uncorrelated failures. SRC_002 provides no causal mechanism operating within a finite horizon; its 'in the limit of infinite time' argument is a limiting argument, not a mechanism. It also assumes the same catastrophic shock affects all nodes 'regardless of topology' without specifying the causal channel — air-gapped or offline nodes would not be affected by an internet backbone failure, a causal distinction its mechanism ignores. Thus it fails to engage the problem's demand for a discriminating causal mechanism.","counterexample":["An air-gapped decentralized node is causally unaffected by an internet backbone failure, so the claim that such events affect all nodes regardless of topology is false under a concrete causal analysis."],"target":"f1d60e094e6f77b649e4e467a0b076ac20ac3cbe593d4e8e564fe39307f08d62"}]}